<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Castillon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1453">1453</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Castillon was fought on 17 July 1453 near Castillon on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dordogne">Dordogne</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>, and is regarded as the last battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. An English army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-talbot-1st-earl-of-shrewsbury">John Talbot</a>, Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a>, attacked a fortified French camp and was destroyed by French artillery, and Talbot was killed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a> surrendered in October, ending three centuries of English rule in Gascony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-castillon.jpg" alt="Battle of Castillon" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ais_5054,_fol._229v,_Bataille_de_Castillon_1453_-_d%C3%A9tail.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>English rule ended after the <b>Battle of Castillon</b> in July 1453, where French artillery broke the English attack and the commander John Talbot, Earl of Shrewsbury, was killed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Duchy of Aquitaine · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>All was lost after the French recovery; defeat at the <b>Battle of Castillon</b> in 1453 left only Calais, which fell in 1558.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Recovery came with Joan of Arc's relief of Orléans in 1429 and with Charles VII's reforms, which in 1445 created the compagnies d'ordonnance, the first permanent royal cavalry, and used artillery to win at Formigny in 1450 and <b>Castillon</b> in 1453.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France · Military</a></li></ul></section>
